{
  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "If you mean device-constituent indexing, the Manual generally calls for capturing the main picture or idea, rather than listing leaves and scrolls that merely form a decorative border.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part5/x-device-constituents/conventional-decorative-elements",
          "quote": "Where decorative elements form a frame or border around significant figures or scenes they are generally not indexed, for example, leaves, arabesques, medals, scrolls."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part5/x-device-constituents/conventional-decorative-elements",
          "quote": "Generally it is the main 'idea' of the mark that is significant and that needs to be captured with the appropriate device constituent terms."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "However, the Manual says decorative elements will be captured where they are the main or only constituents of the trade mark.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part5/x-device-constituents/conventional-decorative-elements",
          "quote": "In the case of trade marks where the decorative elements are the main or only constituents, these elements will be captured."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "I cannot tell from the question alone whether this logo’s leaves and scrolls are merely decorative or are themselves main constituents.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    },
    {
      "text": "The indexing guidance is separate from the Manual’s requirement that the representation show each feature clearly enough for proper examination.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part21/2#1",
          "quote": "The representations must clearly demonstrate the nature of the mark, and show each feature clearly enough to permit proper examination (subregulation 4.3(8))."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you mean a formal description rather than indexing, regulation 4.3(7) requires a concise and accurate description where the trade mark contains or consists of colour, scent, shape, sound, an aspect of packaging, or a combination of those features.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMR1995/r4.3(7)",
          "quote": "(7) If a trade mark for which registration is sought contains or consists of a sign that is a colour, scent, shape, sound or an aspect of packaging, or any combination of those features, the application for registration of the trade mark must include a concise and accurate description of the trade mark."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    }
  ],
  "declined": false,
  "concepts_used": [
    "GC-0072",
    "GC-0073",
    "GC-0038"
  ]
}
